<newsitem itemid="201594" id="root" date="1996-11-19" xml:lang="en">
<title>HONG KONG: Winton interim net down 8.45 percent.</title>
<headline>Winton interim net down 8.45 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended September 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   8.7    vs 9.5 (see note)</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    3.0    vs 3.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil    vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    36.35  vs 39.70 (see note)</p>
<p>    Turnover		     707.50 vs 580.36</p>
<p>    Company name		 Winton Holdings (Bermuda) Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  December 3-6</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   December 12</p>
<p>NOTE - Winton is a taxi-financing and restaurant group.</p>
<p>The comparative figures have been restated to reflect the effect of the change of the accounting policy relating to the recognition of liability on long service payments, which reduced the net profit from HK$43.58 million to HK$39.70 million.</p>
<p>The company has changed its financial year end date to December 31 from March 31 and the next set of audited financial statements will be for a nine-month period from April 1 to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
